<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish mid-Aug consumer prices rise 1.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Irish mid-Aug consumer prices rise 1.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish inflation, as measured by the consumer price index, rose 1.5 percent in the year to mid-August compared with 1.4 percent in the year to mid-May, the Central Statistics Office (CSO) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>		    qtr-on-qtr	    yr-on-yr</p>
<p>    Latest	   +0.5		   +1.5</p>
<p>    Previous	 +0.4		   +1.4</p>
<p>    Year-ago	 +0.4		   +2.4</p>
<p>Market forecasts for annual growth in the CPI had ranged from 1.5 to 1.8 percent.  </p>
<p>The detailed breakdown of the index is as follows:</p>
<p>    Commodity Group     qtr-on-qtr	    yr-on-yr</p>
<p>    Food			 +0.1		   +2.4</p>
<p>    Alcoholic drink	  +2.1		   +3.0</p>
<p>    Tobacco		    unch		   +4.9</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear  -2.3		   -1.4</p>
<p>    Fuel and light	   unch		   +1.8</p>
<p>    Housing		    +0.4		   -2.6</p>
<p>    Durable household goods+0.5		   +1.4</p>
<p>    Other goods		-0.3		   +2.2</p>
<p>    Transport		  -0.4		   +1.4</p>
<p>Services, related</p>
<p>	expenditure	    +2.2		   +0.4</p>
<p>NOTE - The European Union interim index of consumer prices, which is used for intra-EU comparisons, showed a 0.2 percent rise on the quarter for a 2.2 percent increase year-on-year.</p>
<p>The consumer price index excluding mortgage interest, rose by 0.5 percent on the quarter and 1.8 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
